  "description": "I1 probe for prop:jonquiere-cyclotomic-tate-rationality.  Verifies the universal Jonquière closed form Li_n(ζ_K) − (−1)^{n−1} Li_n(ζ_K^{−1}) = −(2πi)^n / n! · B_n(1/K) at K = 2, …, 8 and n = 2, 3, 4, 5 (28 cases).  Max residue 5.43e-71 at the live compute precision (measured 2026-09-13; this field read 'all residues at ~1e-49 (mpmath 50 dps)' until then, which is the precision the corpus ran at when the probe was written, not the one it runs at now).  This identity establishes Tate-rationality of the 'wrong-parity' part of Li_n at primitive K-th roots of unity: Im Li_n(ζ_K) ∈ π^n ℚ for odd n, Re Li_n(ζ_K) ∈ π^n ℚ for even n.",
